# Build a Java 21 Spring Boot 3.4.0 Gradle 8.11.1 REST backend using MySQL through Spring Data JPA/Hibernate for enterprise HR management. Authenticate employees with JWT and authorize requests using exactly the HR, MANAGER, and EMPLOYEE roles. Employees have credentials, a role, optional department and designation assignments, and an optional manager who is another employee; the manager relationship represents the subordinate hierarchy. Provide HR-controlled onboarding, department management, designation management, payroll record management, performance review cycle management, employee manager assignment, and administrative attendance and leave-balance reports. Provide authenticated employee attendance check-in and check-out operations with server-recorded timestamps and retrieval of the caller's attendance. Do not allow a second open attendance record before checkout. Provide leave requests with inclusive start and end dates, a reason, and PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED status. Employees create and view their own requests; managers approve or reject requests for their direct subordinates. Approval must reject overlapping requests and requests whose duration exceeds the employee's remaining annual leave balance. Store each employee's annual leave entitlement and calculate remaining leave as entitlement minus approved leave days. Treat HR as the administrative role for the requested reports because no separate ADMIN role was requested. Expose JSON APIs, validate request bodies, use appropriate HTTP status codes, and return structured API errors for validation, missing-resource, authentication, authorization, and business-rule failures.

Build a Java 21 Spring Boot 3.4.0 Gradle 8.11.1 REST backend using MySQL through Spring Data JPA/Hibernate for enterprise HR management. Authenticate employees with JWT and authorize requests using exactly the HR, MANAGER, and EMPLOYEE roles. Employees have credentials, a role, optional department and designation assignments, and an optional manager who is another employee; the manager relationship represents the subordinate hierarchy. Provide HR-controlled onboarding, department management, designation management, payroll record management, performance review cycle management, employee manager assignment, and administrative attendance and leave-balance reports. Provide authenticated employee attendance check-in and check-out operations with server-recorded timestamps and retrieval of the caller's attendance. Do not allow a second open attendance record before checkout. Provide leave requests with inclusive start and end dates, a reason, and PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED status. Employees create and view their own requests; managers approve or reject requests for their direct subordinates. Approval must reject overlapping requests and requests whose duration exceeds the employee's remaining annual leave balance. Store each employee's annual leave entitlement and calculate remaining leave as entitlement minus approved leave days. Treat HR as the administrative role for the requested reports because no separate ADMIN role was requested. Expose JSON APIs, validate request bodies, use appropriate HTTP status codes, and return structured API errors for validation, missing-resource, authentication, authorization, and business-rule failures.

## Stack
- Language: java 21.0.12.1
- Framework: spring-boot 3.4.0
- Build tool: gradle 8.11.1
- ORM: jpa-hibernate 6.6.2
- Database: mysql 8.4.3

## Entities
### Employee (`employee`)
An authenticated enterprise employee and the root of departmental, designation, and manager-subordinate assignments.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employeeCode: String (required) — Unique enterprise employee identifier.
- fullName: String (required) — Employee display name.
- email: String (required) — Unique login identity.
- passwordHash: String (required) — BCrypt password hash; never returned by API responses.
- role: Role enum (required) — HR, MANAGER, or EMPLOYEE.
- annualLeaveEntitlementDays: Integer (required) — Annual leave allowance used by leave-balance reporting.
- department: Department (optional) — Optional assigned department.
- designation: Designation (optional) — Optional assigned designation.
- manager: Employee (optional) — Optional direct manager.
- Relationships: Many employees may belong to one department., Many employees may have one designation., An employee may have one direct manager and many direct subordinates., An employee owns attendance records, leave requests, and payroll records.

### Department (`department`)
A managed organizational department.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- name: String (required) — Unique department name.
- description: String (optional) — Optional department description.
- Relationships: One department can be assigned to many employees.

### Designation (`designation`)
A managed employee job designation.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- name: String (required) — Unique designation name.
- description: String (optional) — Optional designation description.
- Relationships: One designation can be assigned to many employees.

### AttendanceRecord (`attendance`)
One employee attendance interval containing check-in and optional check-out timestamps.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employee: Employee (required) — Employee who checked in.
- checkInAt: Instant (required) — Server-recorded check-in timestamp.
- checkOutAt: Instant (optional) — Server-recorded checkout timestamp; null while open.
- Relationships: Many attendance records belong to one employee.

### LeaveRequest (`leave_request`)
An employee request for leave with a manager approval workflow.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employee: Employee (required) — Requesting employee.
- startDate: LocalDate (required) — Inclusive leave start date.
- endDate: LocalDate (required) — Inclusive leave end date.
- reason: String (required) — Employee-provided reason.
- status: LeaveStatus enum (required) — PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED.
- reviewedBy: Employee (optional) — Manager who made the decision.
- reviewedAt: Instant (optional) — Decision timestamp.
- Relationships: Many leave requests belong to one employee., A decided leave request references the manager who reviewed it.

### PayrollRecord (`payroll_record`)
An HR-managed payroll record for an employee and payroll period.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employee: Employee (required) — Employee being paid.
- payPeriodStart: LocalDate (required) — Payroll period start date.
- payPeriodEnd: LocalDate (required) — Payroll period end date.
- grossAmount: BigDecimal (required) — Gross payroll amount.
- deductionAmount: BigDecimal (required) — Total deductions.
- netAmount: BigDecimal (required) — Net payroll amount.
- paidAt: Instant (optional) — Optional payment completion timestamp.
- Relationships: Many payroll records belong to one employee.

### PerformanceReviewCycle (`performance_review_cycle`)
An HR-managed named period during which performance reviews occur.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- name: String (required) — Unique cycle name.
- startDate: LocalDate (required) — Cycle start date.
- endDate: LocalDate (required) — Cycle end date.
- description: String (optional) — Optional cycle description.

## Endpoints
- `POST /api/auth/login` — Authenticate with email and password and receive a JWT. (public)
- `POST /api/employees` — HR onboards an employee with credentials, role, leave entitlement, and optional assignments. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/employees/{employeeId}/manager` — HR assigns or clears an employee's direct manager. (auth required)
- `POST /api/departments` — HR creates a department. (auth required)
- `GET /api/departments` — Authenticated users list departments. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/departments/{id}` — HR updates a department. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/departments/{id}` — HR deletes a department that is not assigned to employees. (auth required)
- `POST /api/designations` — HR creates a designation. (auth required)
- `GET /api/designations` — Authenticated users list designations. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/designations/{id}` — HR updates a designation. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/designations/{id}` — HR deletes a designation that is not assigned to employees. (auth required)
- `POST /api/attendance/check-in` — Authenticated employee creates an open attendance record using the current server timestamp. (auth required)
- `POST /api/attendance/check-out` — Authenticated employee closes their open attendance record using the current server timestamp. (auth required)
- `GET /api/attendance/me` — Authenticated employee lists their attendance records. (auth required)
- `POST /api/leave-requests` — Authenticated employee submits a pending leave request. (auth required)
- `GET /api/leave-requests/me` — Authenticated employee lists their leave requests. (auth required)
- `GET /api/leave-requests/pending-subordinates` — Manager lists pending requests from direct subordinates. (auth required)
- `PATCH /api/leave-requests/{id}/decision` — Direct manager approves or rejects a pending subordinate leave request. (auth required)
- `POST /api/payroll-records` — HR creates a payroll record. (auth required)
- `GET /api/payroll-records` — HR lists payroll records. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/payroll-records/{id}` — HR updates a payroll record. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/payroll-records/{id}` — HR deletes a payroll record. (auth required)
- `POST /api/performance-review-cycles` — HR creates a performance review cycle. (auth required)
- `GET /api/performance-review-cycles` — Authenticated users list performance review cycles. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/performance-review-cycles/{id}` — HR updates a performance review cycle. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/performance-review-cycles/{id}` — HR deletes a performance review cycle. (auth required)
- `GET /api/reports/attendance` — HR retrieves attendance report data, optionally filtered by inclusive date range. (auth required)
- `GET /api/reports/leave-balances` — HR retrieves every employee's annual entitlement, approved leave days, and remaining leave balance. (auth required)

