# Build a Java 21 Spring Boot 3.4.0 Gradle 8.11.1 REST backend using MySQL through Spring Data JPA/Hibernate for enterprise HR management. Authenticate employees with JWT and authorize requests using exactly the HR, MANAGER, and EMPLOYEE roles. Employees have credentials, a role, optional department and designation assignments, and an optional manager who is another employee; the manager relationship represents the subordinate hierarchy. Provide HR-controlled onboarding, department management, designation management, payroll record management, performance review cycle management, employee manager assignment, and administrative attendance and leave-balance reports. Provide authenticated employee attendance check-in and check-out operations with server-recorded timestamps and retrieval of the caller's attendance. Do not allow a second open attendance record before checkout. Provide leave requests with inclusive start and end dates, a reason, and PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED status. Employees create and view their own requests; managers approve or reject requests for their direct subordinates. Approval must reject overlapping requests and requests whose duration exceeds the employee's remaining annual leave balance. Store each employee's annual leave entitlement and calculate remaining leave as entitlement minus approved leave days. Treat HR as the administrative role for the requested reports because no separate ADMIN role was requested. Expose JSON APIs, validate request bodies, use appropriate HTTP status codes, and return structured API errors for validation, missing-resource, authentication, authorization, and business-rule failures.

Build a Java 21 Spring Boot 3.4.0 Gradle 8.11.1 REST backend using MySQL through Spring Data JPA/Hibernate for enterprise HR management. Authenticate employees with JWT and authorize requests using exactly the HR, MANAGER, and EMPLOYEE roles. Employees have credentials, a role, optional department and designation assignments, and an optional manager who is another employee; the manager relationship represents the subordinate hierarchy. Provide HR-controlled onboarding, department management, designation management, payroll record management, performance review cycle management, employee manager assignment, and administrative attendance and leave-balance reports. Provide authenticated employee attendance check-in and check-out operations with server-recorded timestamps and retrieval of the caller's attendance. Do not allow a second open attendance record before checkout. Provide leave requests with inclusive start and end dates, a reason, and PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED status. Employees create and view their own requests; managers approve or reject requests for their direct subordinates. Approval must reject overlapping requests and requests whose duration exceeds the employee's remaining annual leave balance. Store each employee's annual leave entitlement and calculate remaining leave as entitlement minus approved leave days. Treat HR as the administrative role for the requested reports because no separate ADMIN role was requested. Expose JSON APIs, validate request bodies, use appropriate HTTP status codes, and return structured API errors for validation, missing-resource, authentication, authorization, and business-rule failures.

## Stack
- Language: java 21.0.12.1
- Framework: spring-boot 3.4.0
- Build tool: gradle 8.11.1
- ORM: jpa-hibernate 6.6.2
- Database: mysql 8.4.3

## Entities
### Employee (`employee`)
An authenticated enterprise employee and the root of departmental, designation, and manager-subordinate assignments.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employeeCode: String (required) — Unique enterprise employee identifier.
- fullName: String (required) — Employee display name.
- email: String (required) — Unique login identity.
- passwordHash: String (required) — BCrypt password hash; never returned by API responses.
- role: Role enum (required) — HR, MANAGER, or EMPLOYEE.
- annualLeaveEntitlementDays: Integer (required) — Annual leave allowance used by leave-balance reporting.
- department: Department (optional) — Optional assigned department.
- designation: Designation (optional) — Optional assigned designation.
- manager: Employee (optional) — Optional direct manager.
- Relationships: Many employees may belong to one department., Many employees may have one designation., An employee may have one direct manager and many direct subordinates., An employee owns attendance records, leave requests, and payroll records.

### Department (`department`)
A managed organizational department.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- name: String (required) — Unique department name.
- description: String (optional) — Optional department description.
- Relationships: One department can be assigned to many employees.

### Designation (`designation`)
A managed employee job designation.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- name: String (required) — Unique designation name.
- description: String (optional) — Optional designation description.
- Relationships: One designation can be assigned to many employees.

### AttendanceRecord (`attendance`)
One employee attendance interval containing check-in and optional check-out timestamps.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employee: Employee (required) — Employee who checked in.
- checkInAt: Instant (required) — Server-recorded check-in timestamp.
- checkOutAt: Instant (optional) — Server-recorded checkout timestamp; null while open.
- Relationships: Many attendance records belong to one employee.

### LeaveRequest (`leave_request`)
An employee request for leave with a manager approval workflow.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employee: Employee (required) — Requesting employee.
- startDate: LocalDate (required) — Inclusive leave start date.
- endDate: LocalDate (required) — Inclusive leave end date.
- reason: String (required) — Employee-provided reason.
- status: LeaveStatus enum (required) — PENDING, APPROVED, or REJECTED.
- reviewedBy: Employee (optional) — Manager who made the decision.
- reviewedAt: Instant (optional) — Decision timestamp.
- Relationships: Many leave requests belong to one employee., A decided leave request references the manager who reviewed it.

### PayrollRecord (`payroll_record`)
An HR-managed payroll record for an employee and payroll period.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- employee: Employee (required) — Employee being paid.
- payPeriodStart: LocalDate (required) — Payroll period start date.
- payPeriodEnd: LocalDate (required) — Payroll period end date.
- grossAmount: BigDecimal (required) — Gross payroll amount.
- deductionAmount: BigDecimal (required) — Total deductions.
- netAmount: BigDecimal (required) — Net payroll amount.
- paidAt: Instant (optional) — Optional payment completion timestamp.
- Relationships: Many payroll records belong to one employee.

### PerformanceReviewCycle (`performance_review_cycle`)
An HR-managed named period during which performance reviews occur.
- id: Long (required) — Database-generated primary key.
- name: String (required) — Unique cycle name.
- startDate: LocalDate (required) — Cycle start date.
- endDate: LocalDate (required) — Cycle end date.
- description: String (optional) — Optional cycle description.

## Endpoints
- `POST /api/auth/login` — Authenticate with email and password and receive a JWT. (public)
- `POST /api/employees` — HR onboards an employee with credentials, role, leave entitlement, and optional assignments. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/employees/{employeeId}/manager` — HR assigns or clears an employee's direct manager. (auth required)
- `POST /api/departments` — HR creates a department. (auth required)
- `GET /api/departments` — Authenticated users list departments. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/departments/{id}` — HR updates a department. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/departments/{id}` — HR deletes a department that is not assigned to employees. (auth required)
- `POST /api/designations` — HR creates a designation. (auth required)
- `GET /api/designations` — Authenticated users list designations. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/designations/{id}` — HR updates a designation. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/designations/{id}` — HR deletes a designation that is not assigned to employees. (auth required)
- `POST /api/attendance/check-in` — Authenticated employee creates an open attendance record using the current server timestamp. (auth required)
- `POST /api/attendance/check-out` — Authenticated employee closes their open attendance record using the current server timestamp. (auth required)
- `GET /api/attendance/me` — Authenticated employee lists their attendance records. (auth required)
- `POST /api/leave-requests` — Authenticated employee submits a pending leave request. (auth required)
- `GET /api/leave-requests/me` — Authenticated employee lists their leave requests. (auth required)
- `GET /api/leave-requests/pending-subordinates` — Manager lists pending requests from direct subordinates. (auth required)
- `PATCH /api/leave-requests/{id}/decision` — Direct manager approves or rejects a pending subordinate leave request. (auth required)
- `POST /api/payroll-records` — HR creates a payroll record. (auth required)
- `GET /api/payroll-records` — HR lists payroll records. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/payroll-records/{id}` — HR updates a payroll record. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/payroll-records/{id}` — HR deletes a payroll record. (auth required)
- `POST /api/performance-review-cycles` — HR creates a performance review cycle. (auth required)
- `GET /api/performance-review-cycles` — Authenticated users list performance review cycles. (auth required)
- `PUT /api/performance-review-cycles/{id}` — HR updates a performance review cycle. (auth required)
- `DELETE /api/performance-review-cycles/{id}` — HR deletes a performance review cycle. (auth required)
- `GET /api/reports/attendance` — HR retrieves attendance report data, optionally filtered by inclusive date range. (auth required)
- `GET /api/reports/leave-balances` — HR retrieves every employee's annual entitlement, approved leave days, and remaining leave balance. (auth required)

## Files
### Wave 1
- `settings.gradle` — Declare the Gradle root project.
  - exports/contract: Sets the root project name to hr-management-api.
  - acceptance: Gradle recognizes the project root.
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/HrManagementApplication.java` — Provide the Spring Boot application entry point.
  - exports/contract: Exports public class HrManagementApplication in package com.enterprise.hr with a standard main method calling SpringApplication.run.
  - acceptance: The class is a valid @SpringBootApplication entry point.
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/domain/HrDomain.java` — Define all JPA entities, role/workflow enums, mappings, constraints, and entity lifecycle data for the HR domain.
  - exports/contract: Exports public JPA entity classes Employee, Department, Designation, AttendanceRecord, LeaveRequest, PayrollRecord, and PerformanceReviewCycle in com.enterprise.hr.domain; exports public enums Role with HR, MANAGER, EMPLOYEE and LeaveStatus with PENDING, APPROVED, REJECTED. Employee has unique employeeCode/email, BCrypt passwordHash, entitlement, optional Department/Designation, and self-referencing optional manager. AttendanceRecord has employee, checkInAt, nullable checkOutAt. LeaveRequest has employee, inclusive dates, reason, status, nullable reviewer/timestamp. PayrollRecord and PerformanceReviewCycle expose the fields described in the specification. Entities provide constructors/getters/setters required by JPA and services without serializing password hashes.
  - acceptance: All seven declared entities are annotated and persistable.; Database uniqueness and non-null constraints enforce required identifiers and workflow data.; Role and leave-status enum values exactly match the specified values.
- `src/main/resources/application.yml` — Provide externalized MySQL, JPA, JWT, and server configuration.
  - exports/contract: Defines datasource URL, username, and password from environment variables with local MySQL defaults; configures Hibernate schema update and MySQL dialect; defines JWT secret and expiration properties configurable by environment; configures JSON error output suitable for API validation failures.
  - acceptance: Application configuration contains no hard-coded production credentials and binds datasource and JWT settings from environment variables.
### Wave 2
- `build.gradle` — Configure the Java 21 Spring Boot Gradle build and required runtime libraries.
  - depends on: settings.gradle
  - exports/contract: Applies Spring Boot 3.4.0 and dependency-management plugins; configures Java 21; provides Spring Web, Validation, Security, Spring Data JPA, MySQL connector, JJWT API/implementation/Jackson modules, and Spring Boot test dependencies; configures JUnit Platform.
  - acceptance: ./gradlew build resolves all dependencies and compiles the project with Java 21.
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/api/HrDtos.java` — Define validated request records and safe response/report records for all HTTP APIs.
  - depends on: src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/domain/HrDomain.java
  - exports/contract: Exports public request/response DTO records in com.enterprise.hr.api for login/token, employee onboarding and manager assignment, department/designation create-update responses, attendance responses, leave creation/decision/responses, payroll create-update/responses, review-cycle create-update/responses, attendance reports, leave-balance reports, and API errors. Requests use Jakarta Validation constraints. Response DTOs never expose Employee.passwordHash. Leave decision input accepts only APPROVED or REJECTED, not PENDING.
  - acceptance: Every mutating endpoint has a typed validated request DTO.; All API response DTOs avoid credential hashes.; DTOs can represent every field required by the declared endpoints and reports.
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/repository/HrRepositories.java` — Define Spring Data repository interfaces and query methods needed by authentication, workflow, reporting, and management services.
  - depends on: src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/domain/HrDomain.java
  - exports/contract: Exports public repository interfaces EmployeeRepository, DepartmentRepository, DesignationRepository, AttendanceRecordRepository, LeaveRequestRepository, PayrollRecordRepository, and PerformanceReviewCycleRepository in com.enterprise.hr.repository. EmployeeRepository supports lookup by email and employee code; AttendanceRecordRepository supports current employee records and an employee's open record; LeaveRequestRepository supports employee requests, pending direct-subordinate requests, approved leave total/date overlap checks, and report retrieval; remaining repositories provide CRUD and required duplicate checks.
  - acceptance: Each repository extends JpaRepository for its corresponding domain entity.; Repository methods support all service operations without exposing raw SQL to controllers.
### Wave 3
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/api/ApiExceptionHandler.java` — Translate application, validation, authentication, and authorization failures into consistent JSON API errors.
  - depends on: src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/api/HrDtos.java
  - exports/contract: Exports public API exception types ResourceNotFoundException and BusinessRuleException plus public @RestControllerAdvice ApiExceptionHandler in com.enterprise.hr.api. It maps validation failures to 400, missing resources to 404, business-rule failures to 409, authentication failures to 401, and authorization failures to 403 using the HrDtos API error response shape.
  - acceptance: Invalid request bodies return structured 400 JSON errors.; Workflow conflicts return 409 and missing entity identifiers return 404.; Security failures have no stack traces or password data in responses.
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/security/JwtSecurity.java` — Implement JWT issuing, JWT request authentication, authenticated employee lookup, password encoding, and route authorization.
  - depends on: src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/domain/HrDomain.java, src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/repository/HrRepositories.java
  - exports/contract: Exports public JwtService with token generation and validation methods, public JwtAuthenticationFilter extending OncePerRequestFilter, and public SecurityConfig exposing PasswordEncoder and SecurityFilterChain beans in com.enterprise.hr.security. JWT subject is employee email and includes the role authority. The filter loads the current Employee through EmployeeRepository. Security is stateless, permits only POST /api/auth/login anonymously, requires authentication elsewhere, and provides role restrictions that controllers may additionally enforce with @PreAuthorize.
  - acceptance: Passwords are checked and encoded with BCrypt.; Valid bearer JWTs establish Spring Security authentication with HR, MANAGER, or EMPLOYEE authority.; Missing or invalid JWTs cannot access protected routes.
### Wave 4
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/service/HrService.java` — Implement all business operations, authorization-sensitive ownership checks, workflow rules, entity mapping, and reporting calculations.
  - depends on: src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/domain/HrDomain.java, src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/repository/HrRepositories.java, src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/api/HrDtos.java, src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/security/JwtSecurity.java
  - exports/contract: Exports public HrService in com.enterprise.hr.service with methods used by HrController for login, onboarding, manager assignment, department/designation CRUD, check-in/out and personal attendance, leave creation/listing/pending-subordinate listing/decision, payroll CRUD, review-cycle CRUD, attendance reports, and leave-balance reports. It accepts and returns HrDtos DTOs, uses repositories, uses PasswordEncoder for onboarding, JwtService for login, and throws defined API exceptions for missing data and invalid business state. It obtains the authenticated employee from SecurityContext. Manager decisions are allowed only for direct subordinates; only PENDING requests are decidable; approved requests must not overlap existing approved requests and must fit remaining entitlement. Check-in/check-out timestamps are Instant.now().
  - acceptance: Service methods enforce the requested role, ownership, manager hierarchy, attendance, and leave workflow rules.; Remaining leave equals entitlement minus approved inclusive leave days.; Deletion of a department or designation assigned to an employee is rejected rather than silently corrupting assignments.
### Wave 5
- `src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/api/HrController.java` — Expose all requested REST endpoints and delegate validated work to HrService.
  - depends on: src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/api/HrDtos.java, src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/service/HrService.java, src/main/java/com/enterprise/hr/security/JwtSecurity.java
  - exports/contract: Exports public @RestController HrController in com.enterprise.hr.api. It defines exactly the declared /api/auth, /api/employees, /api/departments, /api/designations, /api/attendance, /api/leave-requests, /api/payroll-records, /api/performance-review-cycles, and /api/reports routes. It uses @Valid DTO bodies, response status codes appropriate to creation/deletion, and @PreAuthorize restrictions: HR for onboarding, hierarchy, management, payroll, and reports; MANAGER for pending-subordinate and decision routes; any authenticated role for common list, personal attendance, and personal leave routes.
  - acceptance: Every declared endpoint has a matching method, HTTP verb, and path.; Controller methods use validated DTOs and do not access repositories directly.; Role annotations prevent non-HR users from management/reports and non-managers from subordinate approval routes.

