# Java monolith greenfield

Nothing is pre-scaffolded here — the agent writes everything itself. (Contrast [Java microservices](08-java-microservices.md), which pre-scaffolds infra modules before the agent's first token.)

## Build tool handling

One build-tool profile call drives the manifest name, build-check/package commands, jar glob, and a wrapper-bootstrap fragment, threaded through STEP 2 (build config), STEP 7 (start scripts), STEP 10 (build check), STEP 10.5 (linting), and the fix loop. All three build tools — Maven, Gradle, and Ant — are supported here (unlike microservices, where Ant is rejected at intake, see [Request Intake](../../reference/02-request-intake-and-config.md)).

## STEP sequence

Rendered before `EXECUTION`: persona, formatting guard, database/version/port blocks, shell rules, sandbox restriction, config targets, package structure.

| Step | Condition | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | always | Entity design — JPA entities or Mongo documents. Kafka design note if gated. |
| 2 | always | Build + DB config: manifest, `application.properties`, mandatory compiler-release pin, springdoc + forwarded-headers config. Kafka build-config note if gated. |
| 2a | build-tool conditional | Wrapper bootstrap (Gradle / Ant+Ivy / Maven — exactly one renders). |
| 3 | always | DTOs. |
| 4 | `auth.method` | Auth — see [Auth](../../capabilities/auth.md). |
| 5 | always | Repositories + services + controllers + main; mandatory Swagger annotations; pagination inline — see [Pagination](../../capabilities/pagination.md); JPA correctness rule (use the save call's returned id, never call the getter on a transient entity). |
| 5.5 | Kafka gated | Producer/consumer wiring. |
| 6 | always | Seed data. |
| 7 | always | Infra: start scripts, Dockerfile/compose/Makefile per flag — the start script is what STEP 11's own boot verification uses (see [Boot verification](../../capabilities/reports-and-deploy.md#boot-verification-every-mode-every-language)); Dockerfile/compose are deliverables only, never the harness's own verification mechanism. |
| 7b | CI flag | CI workflow. |
| 8 | always | (no-op — falls through to 9). |
| 9 | always | README. |
| 10 | always | Build check, fix all compile errors. |
| 10.5 | linting gated | Linting (checkstyle) — see [Build, Quality & Testing](../../capabilities/build-quality-and-testing.md). |
| 11 | `testing_framework` | Compilation verification / API testing (curl) / JUnit 5 + Mockito (the documented default) — see [Build, Quality & Testing](../../capabilities/build-quality-and-testing.md). |
| 12 | `testing_framework` | Skip / baseline test summary. |
| 13 | always | Summary. |
| 14 | `testing_framework` | Skip / iterative fix loop, max 5. |
| 15 / 15.5 | always | Reports (xlsx + docx), email sub-step right after. |
| 16 | always | Final summary — the true stop condition. |

## Hard safety rules

- Port 8080 protection: "NEVER KILL PORT 8080 — it may be used by other services." The app itself runs on its own allocated `{free_port}`, stopped via `$SERVER_PID` — this is a separate, unrelated port warning.
- No brace expansion in shell commands.
- Stop the server with `kill $SERVER_PID` only. No ngrok — tests run against localhost directly.
- Confined to `output_dir`; this platform's own source must never appear in the generated project.
- Config gating: no refresh/RBAC/websocket infrastructure unless the corresponding flag is set.
- JPA correctness: never call the id getter on a transient entity.

## Completion criteria

Stop only when STEP 16's final summary has been printed. The fix loop (STEP 14) stops when no failures/timeouts remain and every skip is confirmed genuinely untestable, or after 5 iterations with no improvement. `completed` status is additionally gated on the xlsx report — see [Quality Gates](../../reference/07-quality-gates.md).

## Capability hooks

| Capability | Where it lands | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| Kafka | STEP 1 tail → STEP 2 tail → STEP 5.5 → STEP 11 (curl arm only) | `kafka_url` |
| Auth | STEP 4, plus inline notes in STEP 5 and STEP 11 | `auth.method` |
| Pagination | Inline in STEP 5 only | `api.pagination.style` |
| Linting | STEP 10.5, checkstyle only | `linting_tool` |
